<title>UK: Barclays leaps on share buyback plans.</title>
<headline>Barclays leaps on share buyback plans.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Barclays Plc leapt 14-1/2p to 1136-1/2 by 0843 GMT on Wednesday after the banking group said it planned to buy back up to 26 million shares, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The size of the share repurchase surprised some, who anticipated smaller and more frequent purchases.</p>
<p>&quot;That's quite a lot of stock,&quot; said SocGen analyst John Tyce. --London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
